00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:06.970
Welcoming you to "The Nightmare Begins."

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.890
With us here is Jonan Vasquez, creator of the show.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:11.550
- I am the creator.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.090
- The voice of Invader Zim himself, Richard Harvitz.

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.530
- Hi, how's everyone doing today?

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.650
- Wally Wingert, tallest red, and others.

00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:19.940
- Howdy!

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.750
- Andy Berman, voice of Gibb.

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.330
I mean, she's back to you.

00:00:24.330 --> 00:00:27.420
- We've got Danielle Koenig and Ricky Simon.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:28.920
Say hello, Danielle, script coordinator.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:30.000
- Hello, Danielle.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:30.860
more about Gib.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:32.700
The unsung Gib.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.960
I loved Gib.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:35.280
America hates Gib.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:36.260
Gib was my favorite.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.340
America hates Gib.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:39.940
I'll get you, Gib.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:41.320
It's already fallen apart.

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:41.920
I know.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.100
The commentary has fallen apart.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.040
Do it for the Gibber.

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:46.320
The commentary begins.

00:00:46.420 --> 00:00:47.120
Hey, there it is.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:47.940
The nightmare begins.

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:48.540
The nightmare begins.

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.720
This was the first big 3D shot ever.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:51.120
This is awesome.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:51.680
Well, you had to.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.100
Tell us a story about Sean Murray.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:55.120
Anybody?

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:56.120
No?

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.790
He wore a cast facial hair.

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.000
And an incredibly strong calf.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.000
He had the boss.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.000
Incredibly strong cash.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Muscular, muscular cash.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.910
He boarded with his feet.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:05.090
Mm-hmm.

00:01:05.090 --> 00:01:08.170
Now what was that about there when you did that thing?

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.090
What are you talking about?

00:01:09.090 --> 00:01:10.090
That laser thing.

00:01:10.090 --> 00:01:11.090
What are you asking about?

00:01:11.090 --> 00:01:12.090
That's a teleporter.

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:13.090
That's how they get to the planet.

00:01:13.090 --> 00:01:14.090
This looks so unlike anything else on Nick.

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:15.090
It just, wow.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.090
That's amazing, isn't it?

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:17.090
Unbelievable.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:20.960
Way to kill the commentary.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:21.960
Yeah.

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:23.960
Don't say anything good.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:24.970
Hey, there's Zim.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:25.970
Oh, wait, there's Zim.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:26.970
Don't say good things about my show.

00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:27.970
Oh, here we go.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:28.970
There's Zim.

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:29.970
There's Zim.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.000
I'm a real American and just insult my show.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Do it, Ricky. Do that line.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.000
What?

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:35.000
The Invasion.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.000
I only do that behind your back, too.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:36.890
I don't remember it.

00:01:36.890 --> 00:01:37.890
It was just on.

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:38.890
Oh, was it?

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:39.890
Yes.

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:40.890
Ricky's voice.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:41.890
He's the voice of the giant spaceman.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:42.890
I know. How about this?

00:01:42.890 --> 00:01:43.890
This Galactic Conquest is near.

00:01:43.890 --> 00:01:44.890
Everybody rewind your DVD.

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:46.890
Do it now, Ricky.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:47.890
Galactic Conquest?

00:01:47.890 --> 00:01:48.890
No.

00:01:48.890 --> 00:01:49.890
I don't like me.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.890
Oh, Ricky won't perform for us.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:52.820
Here we go.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.700
Should have had 2001 playing here,

00:01:56.700 --> 00:01:58.710
and then the end of that Elvis.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.000
Well, the idea was to get this.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:02.000
them to sort of present themselves as sort of

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:03.940
just, I don't know, sort of like a

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.820
pro-wrestling kind of attitude about

00:02:05.820 --> 00:02:07.960
the tallest. They're not very classy.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.780
They're all showmen, you know?

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.760
They're all showmanship. No substance. Cheesy.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.940
Very tacky showmanship.

00:02:13.450 --> 00:02:15.330
So we had Kevin do, Kevin Manthe, the

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:17.810
composer. He's great. Genius. Awesome.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.680
Had him just do this, you know,

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:21.180
guitars, heavy metal guitars.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.640
Go ahead. Say it. Say it, Wally.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:25.560
See? I told you that language.

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.190
I remember you had like a whole schematic

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:30.000
for how this whole elevator thing

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.670
The creators of LASIK actually saw this and created a whole new thing.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:42.470
I do remember the one thing.

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.070
What?

00:02:43.070 --> 00:02:44.470
What was that thing, Richard?

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.970
Oh, you remember that thing.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:46.770
Oh, that thing.

00:02:46.770 --> 00:02:47.270
Yeah.

00:02:47.270 --> 00:02:48.770
I'm trying to share it.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.770
Yeah.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.470
Are you talking about the thing?

00:02:52.470 --> 00:02:53.770
Oh, yeah.

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:54.770
Oh, the thing.

00:02:54.770 --> 00:02:56.070
Man, I hated that thing.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.070
Yeah.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.000
Although the thing turned out to be a good thing in the end.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.000
Cool map. Cool map.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.000
Yeah.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.690
So, Wally, how did you develop the character of Tall is Dread?

00:03:05.690 --> 00:03:10.690
Well, actually, I understood that I was cast first as Purple, and then they found out that

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.690
Kevin was available, and then they switched us.

00:03:12.690 --> 00:03:13.690
Because Purple was cooler.

00:03:13.690 --> 00:03:15.690
Oh, we couldn't get you to stop crying that day.

00:03:15.690 --> 00:03:16.690
I remember.

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:17.690
I liked when he cried.

00:03:17.690 --> 00:03:18.690
It was a horrible day.

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.690
No, just getting to work with Kevin, of course, was amazing.

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:21.690
Why? Why is that?

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.570
Because he's just funny and spontaneous and just amazing to watch.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.580
He spontaneously combusted during the recording.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.580
He did, actually.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.000
That's why he's not here today.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.620
How many invaders were there actually?

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:32.660
There was something like, I don't know.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.760
I remember I had a specific number of invaders.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.710
They all had names, which is funny because you go online,

00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.910
you see online and they have like, you see kids

00:03:40.910 --> 00:03:43.750
and they create these whole characters for themselves

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.290
like they're Invader Billy or something like that.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:48.990
And it's so pathetic because there aren't any other invaders.

00:03:49.550 --> 00:03:50.590
It's so sad.

00:03:51.680 --> 00:03:53.720
And I want to just crush those kids' dreams

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.460
because I'm like, you're not an invader, man.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.280
You're just not.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:03:58.620
But I don't know where they live.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:00.000
- Yeah.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:01.570
So you would show up at their house?

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:04.570
I would if I could, and just say, "Hey, man, you're living a lie."

00:04:04.570 --> 00:04:05.650
Why would you draw that?

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:08.010
That was Andy. Why would you draw that?

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.950
Oh, that's right. That was the line they couldn't share.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:11.170
Explain the "why would you draw that" line.

00:04:11.170 --> 00:04:13.170
Oh, well, I don't have to explain it. I understood it.

00:04:13.170 --> 00:04:15.110
Other people didn't.

00:04:15.110 --> 00:04:18.410
The idea that they would actually have had a conceptual artist

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:23.110
draw one of their own invaders being mutilated by black people, you know?

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:24.310
My favorite thing is that it--

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:26.560
That's bad for morale.

00:04:26.560 --> 00:04:29.540
Oh, Richard. Richard, uh, Trent's here.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.810
- Now, Richard, you have a story. - I do have a story.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:36.250
- Yeah, this was your first time doing Zim's voice

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.890
for an episode, because the pilot was not you, so...

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:40.810
- That is true. - I just told your story.

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:43.190
- Thank you.

00:04:43.190 --> 00:04:45.700
- Right. Yeah.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:48.990
No, I remember, because two things I remember this,

00:04:48.990 --> 00:04:53.690
was this was my first entree into true screaming.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:55.910
Out of the way!

00:04:55.910 --> 00:04:57.870
But remember, we were about to do this whole passage,

00:04:57.870 --> 00:05:00.000
and it was originally radio...

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:01.800
ants?

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:03.640
Like, radioactive ants?

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:06.340
Well, in the original script, I had it

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.320
as marching like radioactive rubber

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.380
ants. And I think it was just

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:12.520
no reason. It was just kind of nonsense.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:14.300
I just replaced ants

00:05:14.300 --> 00:05:15.820
with pants, and

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:17.680
it's suddenly...

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:20.320
Suddenly, there was like a fight on our hands,

00:05:20.440 --> 00:05:22.660
because, you know, radioactive

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.150
rubber ants make sense, but pants,

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:26.570
that's just being said.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:28.410
We don't want to offend our

00:05:28.410 --> 00:05:30.000
geriatric fan name.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.090
- That's it, let's go home.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.450
- Yeah, that's it.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.730
- Oh, it's still going.

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:40.230
- The show just kind of goes on after this.

00:05:40.230 --> 00:05:42.790
- It was a long trek to get me to this point,

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:43.630
do you remember?

00:05:43.630 --> 00:05:45.710
- Yeah, well, you originally came in, what?

00:05:45.710 --> 00:05:48.310
Was it during the pilot, way before you even

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:49.160
recorded the pilot?

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:51.080
- Give us the first voice that you came up with.

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:51.980
- Oh, wait, everyone shut up, this is cool.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:54.460
Oh, man, giant robot.

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:56.840
This scene originally went on, it wasn't written

00:05:56.840 --> 00:06:00.000
to be this long, but it went on for about, I don't know,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:03.500
It would have extended the episode by about a whole other 30 minutes.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:05.850
It was just the robot running around.

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:10.820
Kyle had done a scene with the robot just mayhem.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:12.300
Kyle Nagy storyboard artist?

00:06:12.440 --> 00:06:12.660
Yes.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:14.200
Wasn't it like getting up on its hands?

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.740
It got up on its head, was break dancing, firing lasers.

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:22.690
Very cool, but just would have just dragged on for way too long.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:24.190
Not dragged, because it was really cool looking.

00:06:24.190 --> 00:06:24.910
Was it actually animated that part?

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:26.250
No, it was storyboarded.

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:28.190
So maybe the storyboards will be on the DVD.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:28.710
Oh.

00:06:29.070 --> 00:06:29.780
Or maybe not.

00:06:30.090 --> 00:06:30.890
Ah, my favorite line.

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:32.030
One of my favorite lines of all time.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:32.630
Jason is giving me the thumbs up.

00:06:32.850 --> 00:06:34.620
Worse or better.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:36.780
I wrote that, you know.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:37.460
I know you did.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:38.360
You're a genius.

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:38.880
Oh, by the way,

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.080
any time you say anything that's good,

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:41.800
dialogue-wise, it's me.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:42.770
Hey, got it.

00:06:43.190 --> 00:06:44.950
Now, Jonan, were you very short as a kid?

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:45.930
Is that what this is all about?

00:06:45.950 --> 00:06:46.490
No, no.

00:06:46.910 --> 00:06:48.510
Although, according to some people,

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:50.310
I'm 5'4".

00:06:50.310 --> 00:06:50.630
Wow.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:51.210
Yeah.

00:06:51.790 --> 00:06:52.810
There's the rubber radio.

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.550
That's one of the rumors I've read.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:55.650
There was the rubber pants, yes.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:56.410
There was the rubber pants.

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:58.660
And what were you asking, Andy?

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:00.000
I was saying, give us what you...

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.000
your original take on Zim was, like, some of the, you know--

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:03.840
- Different voice?

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.780
- Different voices I tried were like this.

00:07:05.780 --> 00:07:08.040
- I don't remember other voices you tried.

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:09.060
- Hey.

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.460
Yeah, hey, everybody, it's me, Zim.

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:13.280
How's it going?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:14.880
- And then you had the Bob Hope version.

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:16.340
- Hey, ain't that wild, everybody?

00:07:16.340 --> 00:07:18.120
It's me.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.580
And Jillian, folks, that's what you're fighting for.

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.420
Isn't she wild?

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.260
- There was the Phyllis Diller version, too, I believe.

00:07:24.260 --> 00:07:25.730
- Ha ha!

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:27.980
I wish Fang were here!

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:29.680
Ha ha ha!

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:30.000
- Wow.

00:07:30.030 --> 00:07:30.810
You're sitting next to him.

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:31.070
Hit him.

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:35.590
By the way, Joey, I prefer the Johnny Carson version myself.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:36.710
Okay, look.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:38.990
This is my resume.

00:07:39.110 --> 00:07:39.890
I need more words.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:46.030
By the way, the sandwich here was an artifact from the cut Digestor sequence.

00:07:46.420 --> 00:07:47.300
Oh, that's right.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:48.940
He was going to have to fight somebody.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:54.250
No, no, he gets the sandwich, and then this sequence had many more trials.

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:57.470
And one of them, it culminates into him having to battle the Digestor.

00:07:57.590 --> 00:07:58.390
It's a giant monster.

00:07:58.750 --> 00:07:59.690
And that was, was that recorded?

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:00.000
I forgot.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.690
- That was boarded, that was boarded as well, yeah.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.250
- That was boarded and animatic-ed.

00:08:03.250 --> 00:08:06.590
- And he offers the digestor a sandwich.

00:08:06.590 --> 00:08:08.150
- And thus triumphed.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.270
- Yeah, you see how we placed it ahead of time?

00:08:10.270 --> 00:08:11.130
You know, that's a-

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.450
- I love that it's okay to-

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.990
- Oh wait, here's the shot that we reuse

00:08:13.990 --> 00:08:15.650
a thousand times during the series.

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:17.490
- I love that it's okay to hit people in the eyes

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:20.290
with lasers, but not have rubber pants.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.370
- Well no, it ended up being okay, it's in the show.

00:08:22.370 --> 00:08:23.160
- Yeah.

00:08:23.160 --> 00:08:23.940
- Well, you get hit.

00:08:23.940 --> 00:08:25.020
- This was the coolest.

00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:25.940
- This was it.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.270
- Hey, don't they have that line,

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:29.630
radioactive rubber pants on a t-shirt now?

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:30.000
- Yes.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.640
See? You see? I knew.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:34.360
Look at what a great entrance.

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:41.030
Coming! I heard them! I actually heard them!

00:08:41.190 --> 00:08:43.530
I was up on the roof, and I heard this transmission was coming through!

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:44.970
Not now, son.

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:46.270
That's a picture of Rob Bumpus.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:47.970
Now, ladies and gentlemen, Roger Bumpus.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:50.780
Now, he was actually like a father to you.

00:08:50.780 --> 00:08:52.940
Roger Bumpus did not actually invent toast.

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.820
Yeah, Roger Bumpus was like a father to me during the series.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:57.470
That was only when it came to discipline.

00:08:57.690 --> 00:08:58.950
Didn't he used to spank you during the recording?

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.000
Well, he gave you an allowance.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.040
He did give me an allowance

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.920
I took it directly from his check

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.240
Did he spank you?

